# Desert Were-Worm: "Whenever you attack with creatures with total power 12 or greater for the first time each turn, untap all
# attacking creatures. After this phase, there is an additional combat phase." and "+2/+0 for each Mountain you control". On
# turn 5 Bot1 has three Mountains (the Worm is a 6/5), a Cyclops of One-Eyed Pass (5/2) and a Memnite (1/1): attacking with all
# three is total power exactly 12, so the trigger untaps them and gives one more combat phase; attacking with the same
# three again there is total power 12 again but not for the first time, so no third combat. Bot2 starts at 40 life: 12 + 12.
# The Worm is the 6/5 it should be (not its printed 0/5), and attacked twice (untapped between).

